<section class="hb-section soft" id="faq"><div class="hb-wrap">
<span class="hb-kicker">SALON MARKETING / ANSWERS</span><h2>Questions salon owners actually ask.</h2>
<div class="hb-faqs"><details><summary>How can a braiding salon get more bookings?</summary><p>Promote the services the salon actually offers, communicate location and booking expectations clearly, and connect inquiries to responsive follow-up and real calendar availability.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can you market knotless, boho and box braids separately?</summary><p>Yes. Each service can have its own creative, landing-page message and qualification questions based on the salon&#x27;s offerings.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can an AI receptionist answer salon calls?</summary><p>A clearly identified AI call assistant can answer approved questions, collect style and timing preferences, and arrange transfer or callback when supported.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can a chatbot handle appointment questions?</summary><p>A website chatbot can explain published services, hours, preparation and booking policies. Staff should handle complex styling decisions and confirm appointments.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can you connect leads to our existing booking system?</summary><p>We review the salon&#x27;s booking software and CRM first, then plan supported integrations and follow-up workflows.</p></details>
<details><summary>Do you guarantee fully booked calendars?</summary><p>No. Booking outcomes depend on demand, pricing, location, capacity, availability, customer experience and consistent follow-up.</p></details></div>
</div></section>

